---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About · Hotlines">
  <article class="prose prose-invert mx-auto max-w-2xl text-fg">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl text-fg">About this project</h1>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      World Emergency & Hotlines is an open directory of every crisis, emergency, and support line we can verify,
      for every country on Earth. We think nobody should have to search in a panic.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-8 text-2xl text-fg">How to use it</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-fg-muted">
      <li>Type a country and a category in the search bar (e.g. "Italy domestic violence").</li>
      <li>Use the interactive world map to explore coverage.</li>
      <li>Every country page lists hotlines with a verification status so you can judge confidence.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-8 text-2xl text-fg">Privacy</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      The natural-language finder runs entirely in your browser. We do not log your queries, your location, or anything
      you type. The emergency banner uses only your browser language — no server call.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-8 text-2xl text-fg">If you're in crisis right now</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted">
      Please call your country's emergency number. In most of Europe this is 112; in the US/Canada 911; in the UK 999;
      in Australia 000. The directory lists many more.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
